title: "Agila Manifesto: Socio-technical Foundations for Software Architecture"
abstract: "An international, open-source socio-technical framework establishing 10 principles grounded in systems theory, queueing models, and Conway's Law for human and AI agent collaboration, with its authoritative canonical anchor in Esperanto."
